  "event": "COMMENT",
  "body": "## Overall\n\nSolid PR. The Zod validation at dispatch, token-efficient default flips, and output shaping controls are all good improvements. The `gradle-get-details` refactor into separate `build*Response` functions is clean. Test coverage is thorough. CI is green across all matrix targets.\n\nThe default flips (compact dump, file-first screenshots, maxDimension 800) are behavioral changes for existing callers — confirm this is going out as a minor version bump.\n\n**Approve with minor suggestions** — see inline comments. None are blockers.",
  "comments": [
    {
      "path": "src/tools/adb-shell.ts",
      "line": 27,
      "side": "RIGHT",
      "body": "**Medium:** When `summarized: true`, the response includes `stdout: \"\"` and `stderr: \"\"`. A caller can't distinguish \"command produced no output\" from \"output was summarized away.\" Consider either omitting these fields or making them optional in the schema when `summarized` is set. Right now it's technically valid per the schema (both are required `z.string()`), just potentially misleading."
    },
    {
      "path": "src/tools/adb-shell.ts",
      "line": 49,
      "side": "RIGHT",
      "body": "**Medium:** `originalStdoutChars` and `originalStderrChars` are returned on every shell call, even when there's no truncation. For a token-efficiency PR, this adds overhead to the most common path (no truncation). Consider only including these when `truncated` is true, or when `maxChars` was requested."
    },
    {
      "path": "src/tools/gradle-get-details.ts",
      "line": 38,
      "side": "RIGHT",
      "body": "**Medium:** `\\bW\\b` will match any standalone \"W\" character in gradle output (e.g., in paths, identifiers, hex values), not just log-level markers. Similarly `\\bE\\b` for errors. This could inflate warn/error counts in summary payloads.\n\nFor gradle output specifically, more anchored patterns like `^w:/gm` or `WARNING:` would be more reliable. The error regex is less affected since it also checks `error:`, `Error:`, and `FAILED`, but the standalone `\\bE\\b` branch has the same issue."
    },
    {
      "path": "src/types/schemas/gradle-get-details-output.ts",
      "line": 84,
      "side": "RIGHT",
      "body": "**Low:** Since you already have `detailType` as a literal discriminator on each variant, `z.discriminatedUnion(\"detailType\", [...])` would be more idiomatic than `z.union` + `.refine()`. It gives you better error messages (\"expected detailType 'logs', got 'errors'\") and Zod can narrow the type automatically. Not a bug — just a potential improvement."
    },
    {
      "path": "tests/tools/output-summary.test.ts",
      "line": 6,
      "side": "RIGHT",
      "body": "**Low:** `context: any` — if there's a mock helper or partial type for `ServerContext` used elsewhere in the test suite, using it here would catch type drift if the context shape changes."
    }
  ]
}

